  "details": "The uploader is throwing a warning for any number of instructions over 512, although the publicly announced Excellent target for operations was stated to be 2000. Is the warning a bug, or is an \"instruction\" different from an \"operation\"? What, then, is an instruction, and why is there a limit of 512?\n\nRelatedly, is the limit of 128 tokens per expression just in the beta, or will this be permanent going forward? If so, it feels worth adding to the docs.",
